From 4e78f35913330cb51a5149e98fbaf8c7a099f6b0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Udhayveer Singh <udhayveersingh@Udhayveer.local>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 17:05:49 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Reconnect when the second hop changes instead of waiting
 for a PING timeout

The LAN gateway on the target network moves traffic between WAN uplinks, and
each move silently kills the established MASQUE flow. --hop-probe sends a
TTL=2 echo towards the endpoint at the given interval and ends the session as
soon as a different router answers. Off by default.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
